#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:10003
#: a53db2869a6d4b9b80f52f7a9733e090
msgid "Measuring Upper-Funnel Impact with PyMC‑Marketing"
msgstr "Midiendo el impacto en la parte superior del embudo con PyMC‑Marketing"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:10005
#: 29d0b37c307d46a78242625b3a9292e8
msgid ""
"This notebook is a practical, end-to-end walkthrough for quantifying the "
"impact of **upper-funnel channels** on a downstream business outcome "
"using **Bayesian Marketing Mix Modeling (MMM)**. We will combine a causal"
" DAG, a transparent data-generating process, and a PyMC-Marketing "
"implementation that respects time dynamics (adstock) and nonlinear "
"response (saturation). The emphasis is on **causal reasoning first**, "
"modeling second."
msgstr ""
"Este cuaderno es una guía práctica y completa para cuantificar el impacto"
" de los **canales de embudo superior** en un resultado comercial "
"posterior utilizando **Modelado de Mezcla de Marketing Bayesiano (MMM)**."
" Combinaremos un DAG causal, un proceso generador de datos transparente y"
" una implementación de PyMC-Marketing que respeta las dinámicas "
"temporales (adstock) y la respuesta no lineal (saturación). El énfasis "
"está en **el razonamiento causal primero**, el modelado segundo."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:10007
#: 9ed41efbe1d1450383745fff438a3045
msgid "What you’ll build (at a glance)"
msgstr "Lo que construirás (a simple vista)"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:10009
#: 565c9298e567410aa3f22087d3d93d6e
msgid ""
"A **PyMC-Marketing MMM** with **Geometric Adstock** and "
"**Michaelis–Menten** saturation for the outcome."
msgstr ""
"Un **PyMC-Marketing MMM** con **Adstock Geométrico** y saturación "
"**Michaelis–Menten** para el resultado."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:10010
#: 525b7d21cf6a4ff699e23bb22c9f036e
msgid ""
"A **mediator model** that links upper-funnel activity to downstream "
"exposure."
msgstr ""
"Un **modelo de mediador** que vincula la actividad de la parte superior "
"del embudo con la exposición posterior."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:10011
#: 3fe380bd0427476282ce42e9b3eb8dd1
msgid ""
"A **simulation-based effect estimator** that converts “what-if” changes "
"in the upper funnel into outcome deltas, with uncertainty."
msgstr ""
"Un **estimador de efectos basado en simulaciones** que convierte los "
"cambios de \"qué pasaría si\" en la parte superior del embudo en deltas "
"de resultados, con incertidumbre."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:10013
#: ecafbfad7095494789ec1b6680a7706d
msgid "Why this matters"
msgstr "Por qué esto es importante"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:10015
#: d8e3ef335c784d4593506cc3e125bd22
msgid ""
"Upper-funnel signals rarely act instantaneously or directly to our target"
" variable. Treating them as simple features in a single regression "
"collapses mediation, ignores carryover, and obscures the operating point "
"where marginal returns live. A causal-first MMM clarifies **where** "
"effects originate."
msgstr ""
"Las señales de embudo superior rara vez actúan de manera instantánea o "
"directa sobre nuestra variable objetivo. Tratarles como características "
"simples en una única regresión colapsa la mediación, ignora el arrastre y"
" oscurece el punto operativo donde residen los rendimientos marginales. "
"Un MMM causal-prioritario aclara **dónde** se originan los efectos."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:10017
#: 6c1eb8d59c0f4cf0a5cb1b11fdfa4fb9
msgid "Who this is for"
msgstr "Para quién es esto"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:10019
#: ed7e01a217fe42f7a03f5b1ec2dfab62
msgid ""
"Analysts and data scientists who need a **defensible** way to attribute "
"upper-funnel investments to outcomes, and who are comfortable with "
"Bayesian inference, time-series structure, and basic causal diagrams."
msgstr ""
"Analistas y científicos de datos que necesitan una forma **defendible** "
"de atribuir inversiones en la parte superior del embudo a resultados, y "
"que se sienten cómodos con la inferencia bayesiana, la estructura de "
"series temporales y diagramas causales básicos."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:10021
#: f2aed3dbf0804450b03d73298d9478de
msgid ""
"By the end, you’ll have a repeatable template for answering the “eternal "
"question” of upper-funnel measurement—not by asking MMM to do everything,"
" but by **aligning MMM with your causal understanding of the marketing "
"system**."
msgstr ""
"Al final, tendrás una plantilla repetible para responder a la “pregunta "
"eterna” de la medición en la parte superior del embudo, no pidiendo a MMM"
" que lo haga todo, sino **alineando MMM con tu comprensión causal del "
"sistema de marketing**."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:10023
#: 862302f887dc4d95905d02293dd6ffd2
msgid "What this notebook covers"
msgstr "Lo que cubre este cuaderno"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:10025
#: c348dee513854168aaabcd5d0dfb4b67
msgid ""
"**Framing the problem:** Why upper-funnel measurement is hard and how "
"naive regressions misattribute lift."
msgstr ""
"**Enmarcando el problema:** Por qué la medición en la parte superior del "
"embudo es difícil y cómo las regresiones ingenuas atribuyen erróneamente "
"el aumento."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:10026
#: b2d57e09e8fd41f68a3be60fa8fda0f2
msgid ""
"**Causal scaffold:** A minimal DAG that separates **drivers**, "
"**mediators**, and **outcomes**, clarifying what the *total* effect "
"means."
msgstr ""
"**Andamiaje causal:** Un DAG mínimo que separa **conductores**, "
"**mediadores** y **resultados**, aclarando lo que significa el *efecto "
"total*."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:10027
#: cbbde56d7e094e69b11ad78bbbde691a
msgid ""
"**Dynamic response modeling:** How **adstock** (carryover) and "
"**saturation** (diminishing returns) shape observable performance."
msgstr ""
"**Modelado de respuesta dinámica:** Cómo el **adstock** (arrastre) y la "
"**saturación** (rendimientos decrecientes) moldean el rendimiento "
"observable."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:10028
#: 3ce8c61a87024832b8c72ca183cbc9f3
msgid "**Two-block estimation strategy:**"
msgstr "**Estrategia de estimación en dos bloques:**"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:10029
#: 54c0c0797b874cad8101283afa218bfc
msgid ""
"A mediator block to translate upper-funnel shifts into lower-funnel "
"impressions."
msgstr ""
"Un bloque de mediador para traducir los cambios en la parte superior del "
"embudo en impresiones en la parte inferior del embudo."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:10030
#: 62f8bebdba5045dd942e6fecc0d898fd
msgid "An outcome block to map those impressions into business impact."
msgstr ""
"Un bloque de resultados para traducir esas impresiones en impacto "
"empresarial."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:10031
#: 661da7c256964de9ad50f3c2a0d9bb68
msgid ""
"**Counterfactual thinking:** Turning interventions on upper-funnel "
"channels into predicted changes in the outcome (g-computation)."
msgstr ""
"**Pensamiento contrafactual:** Convertir intervenciones en canales de "
"embudo superior en cambios predichos en el resultado (g-cálculo)."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:10032
#: 2e4625a23b5d43fa904ffc656bcdb543
msgid ""
"**Model checking:** Posterior predictive checks and sanity tests that "
"prevent self-deception."
msgstr ""
"**Verificación de modelos:** Comprobaciones predictivas posteriores y "
"pruebas de cordura que previenen la autoengaño."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:10033
#: 887c90f07cfa4a98a073758186b1c099
msgid ""
"**Reporting effects:** Impulse responses, cumulative lift, and state-"
"dependent elasticities that decision-makers can use."
msgstr ""
"**Efectos de informes:** Respuestas al impulso, aumento acumulativo y "
"elasticidades dependientes del estado que los tomadores de decisiones "
"pueden utilizar."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:10036
#: 4e2285a070e14261a237b147c40461a8
msgid "Business Challenge: Untangling Upper → Mid → Lower Funnel Effects"
msgstr ""
"Desafío de negocio: desentrañando los efectos del embudo superior → medio → "
"inferior"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:10038
#: 56e25a5c13f943b187cdb8faee36c3db
msgid ""
"A consumer brand invests heavily in awareness (video, influencers, PR). "
"Leadership sees short-term sales plateauing and asks: *“Are our upper-"
"funnel dollars doing anything?”* Standard dashboards show weak "
"contemporaneous relations, and channel teams argue that “it all pays back"
" later.” We need a defensible way to quantify how **upper-funnel "
"exposure** propagates through **mid-funnel engagement** to **lower-funnel"
" conversions**—without relying on feelings or opinions only."
msgstr ""
"Una marca de consumo invierte fuertemente en la concienciación (video, "
"influencers, relaciones públicas). La dirección observa que las ventas a "
"corto plazo se estancan y pregunta: *“¿Están nuestros dólares de la parte"
" superior del embudo haciendo algo?”* Los paneles de control estándar "
"muestran relaciones contemporáneas débiles, y los equipos de canal "
"argumentan que “todo se recupera más tarde.” Necesitamos una forma "
"defendible de cuantificar cómo **la exposición en la parte superior del "
"embudo** se propaga a través del **compromiso en la parte media del "
"embudo** hasta las **conversiones en la parte inferior del embudo**—sin "
"depender únicamente de sentimientos u opiniones."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:10040
#: 272f02bd50984f95bbb91efa8cfa0da0
msgid ""
"We start by sketching the world we believe we operate in: a small causal "
"story that will guide every modeling decision that follows."
msgstr ""
"Comenzamos esbozando el mundo en el que creemos que operamos: una pequeña"
" historia causal que guiará cada decisión de modelado que siga."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:30002
#: c905dc140b314d6a923cdde92f94628f
msgid "The Ecosystem based on the Causal DAG"
msgstr "El ecosistema basado en el DAG causal"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:30004
#: 03f9cff6a6ca4d3db0c07c97bc9450d3
msgid "The previous DAG shows three types of effects on it."
msgstr "El DAG anterior muestra tres tipos de efectos sobre él."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:30006
#: 83de353d76d64fbea6c5565fae4d4e4d
msgid ""
"$X1$ **Upper funnel (Awareness impressions):**   Broad reach media (e.g.,"
" online video, display, influencer bursts). Drives *latent consideration*"
" and brand memory, not immediate purchases."
msgstr ""
"$X1$ **Parte superior del embudo (Impresiones de conocimiento):** Medios "
"de amplio alcance (por ejemplo, video en línea, display, ráfagas de "
"influencers). Genera *consideración latente* y memoria de marca, no "
"compras inmediatas."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:30009
#: 1d754150dc394d8b8f0f7d4d175d2356
msgid "$X2$ & $X3$ **Mid funnel (Consideration touchpoints):**"
msgstr "$X2$ y $X3$ **Embudo medio (puntos de contacto de consideración):**"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:30010
#: 8cc86639fc6d452a8d7fa1ecb8d35eb1
msgid "$X2$: Social media impressions / site landings (people start looking)."
msgstr ""
"$X2$: Impresiones en redes sociales / llegadas al sitio (las personas "
"empiezan a buscar)."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:30011
#: e58559f90ca24c9f806e6f2c3bd09a3a
msgid ""
"$X3$: Remarketing impressions (people re-engage after a first touch).   "
"These are **mediators**—they translate awareness into actionable intent."
msgstr ""
"$X3$: Impresiones de remarketing (personas que vuelven a involucrarse "
"después de un primer contacto). Estos son **mediadores**—traducen la "
"conciencia en una intención accionable."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:30014
#: ae1c296ba9a24311be21d2752689fa32
msgid ""
"$X4$ **Lower funnel (High-intent exposures):**   Brand search. These are "
"the **proximal drivers** of the commercial outcome."
msgstr ""
"$X4$ **Embudo inferior (Exposiciones de alta intención):** Búsqueda de "
"marca. Estos son los **impulsores proximales** del resultado comercial."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:30017
#: 38f6928f6d68491bacc8dc728c2db1ad
msgid ""
"*U1*, *U4* **Exogenous shocks:**   Competitor moves, Budgets allocated to"
" teams, or market dynamics changes can perturb each node separately."
msgstr ""
"*U1*, *U4* **Choques exógenos:**   Los movimientos de los competidores, "
"los presupuestos asignados a los equipos o los cambios en la dinámica del"
" mercado pueden perturbar cada nodo por separado."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:30020
#: 359c658830c04e2f8643ed5fe846e4ab
msgid ""
"Traditional MMMs often toss all channels into one regression and look for"
" a global fit. For upper funnel channels, that approach can:"
msgstr ""
"Los MMM tradicionales a menudo combinan todos los canales en una sola "
"regresión y buscan un ajuste global. Para los canales de la parte "
"superior del embudo, ese enfoque puede:"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:30021
#: b6173b34e2a74217b7fb3ea334b4098e
msgid "**Under-credit X1** (because its effect is indirect and delayed)"
msgstr "**Subcrédito X1** (porque su efecto es indirecto y retrasado)"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:30022
#: 5f744dbd062742ecb5fbead0ee8a253c
msgid "**Overfit to X4** (because it is nearest to the outcome)"
msgstr "**Sobreajustar a X4** (porque es el más cercano al resultado)"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:30024
#: a571c95326bd4de98a16999b4a8a1934
msgid "The Business Questions"
msgstr "Las Preguntas Empresariales"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:30026
#: 4f0c39abd2764a29b9d80d1edbd3bfad
msgid ""
"**Q1.** How much does a marginal change in *awareness* (X1) ultimately "
"shift the outcome, via the funnel?"
msgstr ""
"**Q1.** ¿Cuánto cambia un cambio marginal en *conciencia* (X1) el "
"resultado, a través del embudo?"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:30027
#: 5f0b19ade5a3419583e849d4aec12f5c
msgid ""
"**Q2.** Where are we on the **response curve** (are we close to "
"saturation)?"
msgstr ""
"**Q2.** ¿Dónde estamos en la **curva de respuesta** (¿estamos cerca de la"
" saturación)?"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:30028
#: 981c327a108b4da5a5e0d80d067291b7
msgid ""
"**Q3.** What is the expected **cumulative lift** from a planned upper-"
"funnel flight?"
msgstr ""
"**Q3.** ¿Cuál es el **incremento acumulado** esperado de una campaña "
"planificada en la parte superior del embudo?"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:30030
#: fcdb70699a744bcf99cacfc1289e5736
msgid ""
"Nevertheless solve those business questions will not be easy if you don't"
" know anything about causality, as soon you will learn."
msgstr ""
"Sin embargo, resolver esas preguntas de negocio no será fácil si no sabes "
"nada de causalidad, como pronto aprenderás."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:30032
#: c1bfabbaa3d8462b8e8d623644d0cbfd
msgid "Imports"
msgstr "Importaciones"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:30034
#: d7f6c618cc474966b977049efa788b7a
msgid ""
"We’ll work with PyMC-Marketing for MMM components, ArviZ for diagnostics,"
" and Pytensor to keep our simulator honest."
msgstr ""
"Trabajaremos con PyMC-Marketing para los componentes de MMM, ArviZ para "
"diagnósticos y Pytensor para mantener nuestro simulador honesto."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:50002
#: e05a018e615941ef9800881876e12fb0
msgid "Notebook settings"
msgstr "Configuración del cuaderno"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:50003
#: 8de83e9ef72d456396049eff826668ae
msgid ""
"To keep figures consistent and runs reproducible, we lock a seed and a "
"plotting style."
msgstr ""
"Para mantener las cifras consistentes y las ejecuciones reproducibles, "
"bloqueamos una semilla y un estilo de trazado."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:70002
#: ec432d05a6344de2970f5f81d7342acb
msgid "Data generation process"
msgstr "Proceso de generación de datos"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:70004
#: 3858d33850e744fdb9a7925e8d4f798e
msgid ""
"Based on the previous DAG, we will simulate data in pytensor. During this"
" simulation, we explicitly define the relationships between nodes for the"
" model."
msgstr ""
"Con base en el DAG anterior, simularemos datos en pytensor. Durante esta "
"simulación, definimos explícitamente las relaciones entre los nodos del "
"modelo."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:70006
#: 9a6bb779712f4d71bb848b78e9b11c52
msgid ""
"We model these relationships as additive at each node, allowing for a "
"nonlinear response only in the final mapping from lower-funnel exposure "
"to the outcome. Assuming time is indexed by $t=1,\\dots,T$, the resulting"
" structural causal equation is as follows."
msgstr ""
"Modelamos estas relaciones como aditivas en cada nodo, permitiendo una "
"respuesta no lineal únicamente en el mapeo final de la exposición del embudo"
" inferior al resultado. Suponiendo que el tiempo está indexado por "
"$t=1,\\dots,T$, la ecuación causal estructural resultante es la siguiente."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:70008
#: eaf882fef97e40bea317e3955044c09c
msgid "Structural causal equations"
msgstr "Ecuaciones causales estructurales"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:70010
#: 36c72dca56474919a3ca8dee080b607e
msgid ""
"Let $X_1$ (upper funnel), $X_2,X_3$ (mid funnel), $X_4$ (lower funnel), "
"$E_t$ (event),  and $Y$ (business outcome). Exogenous shocks $U_j$ enter "
"additively."
msgstr ""
"Sean $X_1$ (embudo superior), $X_2,X_3$ (embudo medio), $X_4$ (embudo "
"inferior), $E_t$ (evento) y $Y$ (resultado de negocio). Los choques exógenos"
" $U_j$ entran de forma aditiva."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:70012
#: 703638586a994beab906980f85617a70
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"X_{1,t} &= \\mu_{1,t} +  \\beta_{0}\\ E_t \\\\\n"
"X_{2,t} &= \\mu_{2,t} + \\beta_{12}\\,X_{1,t} \\\\\n"
"X_{3,t} &= \\mu_{3,t} + \\beta_{13}\\,X_{1,t} \\\\\n"
"X_{4,t} &= \\mu_{4,t} + \\beta_{24}\\,X_{2,t} + \\beta_{34}\\,X_{3,t}\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
msgstr ""
"\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"X_{1,t} &= \\mu_{1,t} +  \\beta_{0}\\ E_t \\\\\n"
"X_{2,t} &= \\mu_{2,t} + \\beta_{12}\\,X_{1,t} \\\\\n"
"X_{3,t} &= \\mu_{3,t} + \\beta_{13}\\,X_{1,t} \\\\\n"
"X_{4,t} &= \\mu_{4,t} + \\beta_{24}\\,X_{2,t} + \\beta_{34}\\,X_{3,t}\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:70021
#: ac9582da9b3b43199e6a1f647da94590
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"$\\mu_{j,t}$ are the exogenous components of the impressions (e.g: those "
"changes not dependent on other nodes)."
msgstr ""
"$\\mu_{j,t}$ son los componentes exógenos de las impresiones (por "
"ejemplo: aquellos cambios que no dependen de otros nodos)."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:70023
#: aaca76d00ab6472ab32cb2c83a0eff71
msgid "Outcome variable"
msgstr "Variable de resultado"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:70025
#: a0511cb045ac4fddb81a8538c7d030c6
msgid ""
"Let $f(\\cdot)$ denote the nonlinear response function (e.g., Geometric "
"Adstock, Michaelis–Menten). The outcome combines transformed lower-funnel"
" pressure with additive controls:"
msgstr ""
"Sea $f(\\cdot)$ la función de respuesta no lineal (por ejemplo, Geometric"
" Adstock, Michaelis–Menten). El resultado combina la presión transformada"
" del embudo inferior con controles aditivos:"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:70027
#: 2d77f62dffce4d74a3015295861c4eb1
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"\n"
"Y_t \\;=\\; f\\!\\big(X_{4_t};\\,\\theta\\big) \\;+\\; \\text{Trend}_t "
"\\;+\\; \\text{Events}_t \\;+\\; \\varepsilon_t,\n"
msgstr ""
"\n"
"Y_t \\;=\\; f\\!\\big(X_{4_t};\\,\\theta\\big) \\;+\\; \\text{Trend}_t "
"\\;+\\; \\text{Events}_t \\;+\\; \\varepsilon_t,\n"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:70031
#: c6efbeea5f4b41e78a06f1b7f3a98558
#, python-brace-format
msgid "$\\text{Trend}_t$: smooth baseline evolution."
msgstr "$\\text{Trend}_t$: evolución suave de la línea base."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:70032
#: 3e70116186b0493b9f4744b365ae1137
#, python-brace-format
msgid "$\\text{Events}_t$: superposition of localized event basis functions."
msgstr ""
"$\\text{Events}_t$: superposición de funciones base de eventos "
"localizados."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:70033
#: a657f2e5a8f54335840a62109712cbc8
msgid ""
"$\\theta$: parameters of the nonlinear response function (e.g., "
"saturation/adstock)."
msgstr ""
"$\\theta$: parámetros de la función de respuesta no lineal (por ejemplo, "
"saturación/adstock)."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:70035
#: 378969b210d745bca5912251c27717a9
msgid ""
"**Summary:** We assume additive structure at each node, linear mediation "
"$X_1\\!\\to\\!(X_2,X_3)\\!\\to\\!X_4$, dynamic carryover on $X_4$ via "
"adstock, and a nonlinear mapping $f$ from adstocked exposure to $Y$, plus"
" additive trend/events and noise."
msgstr ""
"**Resumen:** Asumimos una estructura aditiva en cada nodo, mediación "
"lineal $X_1\\!\\to\\!(X_2,X_3)\\!\\to\\!X_4$, transferencia dinámica en "
"$X_4$ a través de adstock, y un mapeo no lineal $f$ de la exposición "
"adstocked a $Y$, además de una tendencia/eventos aditivos y ruido."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:80002
#: 005ffd5e16ca42cfa9fb90c024612fe8
msgid ""
"Our story unfolds day by day; we create a daily timeline with a few "
"simple calendar features."
msgstr ""
"Nuestra historia se desarrolla día a día; creamos una línea de tiempo "
"diaria con algunas características de calendario simples."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:100002
#: a28c78af1e484b49978839aa8f840ee0
msgid ""
"Using [PyTensor](https://github.com/pymc-devs/pytensor), we can "
"symbolically represent the causal Directed Acyclic Graph (DAG) in an "
"abstract way before diving into any actual computation."
msgstr ""
"Usando [PyTensor](https://github.com/pymc-devs/pytensor), podemos "
"representar simbólicamente el Grafo Acíclico Dirigido (DAG) causal de manera"
" abstracta antes de sumergirnos en cualquier cálculo real."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:100005
#: 76cc9e95613b4783885bbf13d9f6f480
msgid "What is PyTensor?"
msgstr "¿Qué es PyTensor?"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:100007
#: 80577e5d4e8b44e394eb7ddaac430c49
msgid ""
"PyTensor is a Python library that allows one to define, optimize, and "
"efficiently evaluate mathematical expressions involving multi-dimensional"
" arrays. It provides the computational backend for PyMC."
msgstr ""
"PyTensor es una biblioteca de Python que permite definir, optimizar y "
"evaluar de manera eficiente expresiones matemáticas que involucran arreglos "
"multidimensionales. Proporciona el backend computacional de PyMC."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:100009
#: 5e541e7d86f14ad781ba797ff799560c
msgid ""
"In essence, PyTensor allow us to define static computational graphs, that"
" can be compiled into different backends, like Numba or JAX."
msgstr ""
"En esencia, PyTensor nos permite definir grafos computacionales estáticos, "
"que pueden compilarse en diferentes backends, como Numba o JAX."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:100012
#: 6524b67fd26e4a758b98e3f39c8f0629
msgid ""
"This framework allows us to clearly define the relationships that our "
"data generation process must adhere to. PyTensor simplifies this task and"
" enables us to visualize the resulting graphical model—though it’s a "
"computational DAG rather than a causal one—helping us to confirm that the"
" entire process aligns with our expectations."
msgstr ""
"Este marco nos permite definir claramente las relaciones a las que debe "
"adherirse nuestro proceso de generación de datos. PyTensor simplifica esta "
"tarea y nos permite visualizar el modelo gráfico resultante—aunque se trata "
"de un DAG computacional en lugar de uno causal—ayudándonos a confirmar que "
"todo el proceso se alinea con nuestras expectativas."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:120002
#: 40151e30b4f846ba8e8368f20feba030
msgid ""
"Take a quick glance at the computational graph so we don’t fool "
"ourselves: the ingredients combine exactly as intended. Next, we write "
"down how awareness spills into consideration and then into high‑intent "
"exposures. These links are simple—by design—so we can focus on the causal"
" path rather than curve fitting."
msgstr ""
"Echemos un vistazo rápido al gráfico computacional para no engañarnos: "
"los ingredientes se combinan exactamente como se pretende. A "
"continuación, anotamos cómo la conciencia se transforma en consideración "
"y luego en exposiciones de alta intención. Estos vínculos son simples—por"
" diseño—para que podamos centrarnos en la ruta causal en lugar de ajustar"
" curvas."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:140002
#: 3b10c2a2cdee42f5acc431d83337d372
msgid "Creating the data for our symbolic place holders."
msgstr "Creando los datos para nuestros marcadores de posición simbólicos."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:140004
#: 7de6c4cd5b744f36a3af352c5cbcc672
msgid ""
"First, we kick-off filling in the values for our event and trend "
"variables. Then we craft a gently rising baseline, sprinkle in Gaussian "
"event pulses, and add a whisper of noise."
msgstr ""
"Primero, comenzamos a llenar los valores para nuestras variables de "
"evento y tendencia. Luego, creamos una línea base que sube suavemente, "
"añadimos pulsos de evento gaussianos y agregamos un susurro de ruido."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:160002
#: 29d6caff64114ab2829b4e4525b4c3ad
msgid "We plot the pieces before we mix them."
msgstr "Colocamos las piezas antes de mezclarlas."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:180002
#: 64b6fe6c6fb5496c84dd3d538f19fde8
msgid ""
"We'll simulate our media variables (e.g: Impressions) as random walks. "
"Upper, mid, and lower‑funnel exposures don’t typically jump randomly; "
"they meander around a consistent value. A bounded random walk captures "
"that inertia."
msgstr ""
"Simularemos nuestras variables de medios (por ejemplo: Impresiones) como "
"caminatas aleatorias. Las exposiciones en la parte superior, media e "
"inferior del embudo no suelen saltar aleatoriamente; se deslizan "
"alrededor de un valor consistente. Una caminata aleatoria acotada captura"
" esa inercia."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:200002
#: 8a73df8efff143bdb85246afd372f384
msgid ""
"We let each stream wander within bounds and take a first look at the "
"behavior."
msgstr ""
"Dejamos que cada flujo deambule dentro de los límites y eche un primer "
"vistazo al comportamiento."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:220002
#: e769bb54ff554dbfac9a529b22034463
msgid ""
"Now, we need to define the strength of the relationships, those will be "
"the betas of every variable over the other. Doing so, we can create all "
"missing nodes."
msgstr ""
"Ahora, necesitamos definir la fuerza de las relaciones, esas serán las "
"betas de cada variable sobre las otras. Al hacerlo, podemos crear todos "
"los nodos que faltan."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:240002
#: d39ae8fcdae0434ea1400aed63b48117
msgid ""
"Only `X4` reaches the outcome in our story. That’s where we add memory "
"(adstock) and diminishing returns (saturation)."
msgstr ""
"Solo `X4` alcanza el resultado en nuestra historia. Ahí es donde añadimos"
" memoria (adstock) y rendimientos decrecientes (saturación)."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:270002
#: 1d701caeee6949ff8ca7df71025aaee8
msgid "With everything in place, we can evaluate the target variable."
msgstr "Con todo en su lugar, podemos evaluar la variable objetivo."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:290002
#: 1da2be7498064f918633c056517c4cd6
msgid ""
"We package our story into a single pandas dataframe with features, "
"controls, and the outcome."
msgstr ""
"Empacamos nuestra historia en un único dataframe de pandas con "
"características, controles y el resultado."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:310002
#: 6ab6da6c55564627b38574c2e45eae91
msgid "Train & Test split"
msgstr "División en entrenamiento y prueba"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:310004
#: 2bbdc0c2b36546d3ae337fc6e0dd0c6a
msgid ""
"We keep a holdout to test whether our counterfactual story travels beyond"
" the training window."
msgstr ""
"Mantenemos un grupo de retención para probar si nuestra historia "
"contrafactual se extiende más allá de la ventana de entrenamiento."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:330002
#: d12ddbd6d96c4b8d8d779f9c19787d29
msgid "All-in causal MMM"
msgstr "MMM causal todo en uno"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:330004
#: e0934876d7e04b5d9148a58f9c737be5
msgid ""
"**What this is.** A single MMM with *all* channels modeled as if they "
"directly affect $Y$. Each channel uses Geometric Adstock + "
"Michaelis–Menten saturation; the likelihood is censored Normal. This "
"strategy is very common, basically reflecting the put-it-all-into-the-"
"blender approach."
msgstr ""
"**Qué es esto.** Un único MMM con *todos* los canales modelados como si "
"afectaran directamente a $Y$. Cada canal utiliza Adstock Geométrico + "
"saturación de Michaelis–Menten; la probabilidad es Normal censurada. Esta"
" estrategia es muy común, reflejando básicamente el enfoque de mezclarlo "
"todo en la licuadora."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:350002
#: cecde5aad1ef4b0d8d862b0c2d0f47b1
msgid "Model configuration"
msgstr "Configuración del modelo"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:350004
#: 0500ac554c354ab59a2a747d214e4b2b
msgid ""
"We can define the model priors for every part, saturation and adstock as "
"usual for pymc-marketing models."
msgstr ""
"Podemos definir los priors del modelo para cada parte, saturación y "
"adstock como es habitual en los modelos de pymc-marketing."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:370002
#: 6a8d9d1dab974bd18a01ce8d60adc55e
msgid ""
"Doing the same, we can define the Prior for the likelihood. We set a "
"censored Normal likelihood (no negatives) and sampling defaults that "
"behave well in practice."
msgstr ""
"Haciendo lo mismo, podemos definir el Prior para la verosimilitud. "
"Establecemos una verosimilitud Normal censurada (sin negativos) y valores"
" predeterminados de muestreo que se comportan bien en la práctica."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:390002
#: e8ff6ac4de3b4648ba0306e3b011ae50
msgid ""
"With the config ready, we build the all‑in model and draw from its "
"posterior."
msgstr ""
"Con la configuración lista, construimos el modelo integral y extraemos de"
" su posterior."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:410002
#: c8e68adfb88347f6b819eb56b04e5efb
msgid "Fit model"
msgstr "Ajuste del modelo"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:410004
#: 77237756cef94e7283a2b967bf82d50b
msgid ""
"We also generate posterior predictions to peek at in‑sample recover "
"effects."
msgstr ""
"También generamos predicciones posteriores para vislumbrar los efectos de"
" recuperación en la muestra."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:430002
#: 2d0239133cc2419f839b0cd04ff32487
msgid ""
"Oh! We can see the model already is getting troubles exploring the "
"parameter space and diverging."
msgstr ""
"Oh! Podemos ver que el modelo ya está teniendo problemas para explorar el"
" espacio de parámetros y está divergiendo."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:430004
#: 8ed399f0a83f4bcb8be9938730ed155b
msgid ""
"Nevertheless, let's go directly to the question: **Can the model recover "
"the true contribution if we were not spending anything at all in X1?**"
msgstr ""
"Sin embargo, vayamos directamente a la pregunta: **¿Puede el modelo "
"recuperar la verdadera contribución si no estuviéramos gastando nada en "
"X1?**"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:430006
#: 58334c33db08461699ce0095e64bc133
msgid ""
"We can use the `plot.contributions_over_time` and get the contribution "
"output to find out. If the blender was enough, it would recover the true "
"`X1` contribution. Let's check."
msgstr ""
"Podemos utilizar `plot.contributions_over_time` y obtener la salida de "
"contribuciones para averiguarlo. Si el mezclador fue suficiente, "
"recuperaría la verdadera contribución `X1`. Verifiquemos."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:450002
#: 3fe7f5d36b334b4787fb8edebdc9e99a
msgid ""
"This is great, but we need to get the real contribution if x1 (We can "
"compute it from our pytensor graph, assuming it was zero and taking that "
"from target)."
msgstr ""
"Esto es genial, pero necesitamos obtener la contribución real si x1 "
"(Podemos calcularlo a partir de nuestro gráfico de pytensor, asumiendo "
"que era cero y tomando eso del objetivo)."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:470002
#: 8dbf285468324621ac0e44f14f118972
msgid "Now that we have both, we can compare."
msgstr "Ahora que tenemos ambos, podemos comparar."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:490002
#: ae290cd909ed4cfb86b857620dbd93f3
msgid ""
"As expected, put-it-all-in-the blender overestimates the upper funnel "
"effects. But why the naïve approach fails?"
msgstr ""
"Como era de esperar, poner-todo-en-la-licuadora sobreestima los efectos "
"del embudo superior. Pero, ¿por qué falla el enfoque ingenuo?"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:490004
#: 5542bc5e43904e039d43601c8a3ef262
msgid "Learning about regression assumptions"
msgstr "Aprender sobre los supuestos de la regresión"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:490006
#: 49ca62a34efb4a4bb99829e310a7acff
msgid ""
"When we fit a model including all variables ($X_1, X_2, X_3, X_4, Y$), we"
" observed that the coefficient linking $X_1$ to $Y$ was **too large**. "
"This happens because the model does not respect the **causal structure** "
"defined by our structural equations."
msgstr ""
"Cuando ajustamos un modelo que incluye todas las variables ($X_1, X_2, "
"X_3, X_4, Y$), observamos que el coeficiente que vincula $X_1$ con $Y$ "
"era **demasiado grande**. Esto sucede porque el modelo no respeta la "
"**estructura causal** definida por nuestras ecuaciones estructurales."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:490008
#: c8783757d4c7437b9ed57cd93f9a8953
msgid "The true causal mechanism"
msgstr "El verdadero mecanismo causal"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:490010
#: bc521264f81e44c7801608d394a417b6
msgid ""
"In our data-generating process, $X_1$ does **not** directly affect $Y$. "
"Its influence passes entirely through the sequence:"
msgstr ""
"En nuestro proceso de generación de datos, $X_1$ **no** afecta "
"directamente a $Y$. Su influencia pasa completamente a través de la "
"secuencia:"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:490012
#: aa53fbfb06e24a9ab4c304bfe5b508a3
msgid ""
"\n"
"X_1 \\to (X_2, X_3) \\to X_4 \\to Y\n"
msgstr ""
"\n"
"X_1 \\to (X_2, X_3) \\to X_4 \\to Y\n"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:490016
#: fbf19897a48040a0a055c5597d069ef0
msgid ""
"Each link adds its contribution, and the final step ($X_4 \\to Y$) can be"
" **nonlinear** (for example, showing saturation or adstock effects)."
msgstr ""
"Cada enlace añade su contribución, y el paso final ($X_4 \\to Y$) puede "
"ser **no lineal** (por ejemplo, mostrando efectos de saturación o "
"adstock)."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:490018
#: 6a5a328983ff48559bea81305f0d8ade
msgid ""
"The real total effect of $X_1$ on $Y$ depends on how much $X_1$ changes "
"$X_4$ and how sensitive $Y$ is to $X_4$. Symbolically,"
msgstr ""
"El efecto total real de $X_1$ sobre $Y$ depende de cuánto $X_1$ cambie "
"$X_4$ y de cuán sensible sea $Y$ a $X_4$. Simbólicamente,"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:490020
#: 8d10fc7abfc9431d90438c7ac6e38f18
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"\n"
"\\text{Total effect of } X_1 \\text{ on } Y\n"
"\\;\\propto\\;\n"
"\\text{(effect of } X_1 \\text{ on } X_4)\\;\n"
"\\times\\;\n"
"\\text{(sensitivity of } Y \\text{ to } X_4).\n"
msgstr ""
"\n"
"\\text{Total effect of } X_1 \\text{ on } Y\n"
"\\;\\propto\\;\n"
"\\text{(effect of } X_1 \\text{ on } X_4)\\;\n"
"\\times\\;\n"
"\\text{(sensitivity of } Y \\text{ to } X_4).\n"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:490028
#: cb9c1c95716c4be19e507d14009228ff
msgid ""
"A regression that includes both $X_1$ and $X_4$ as predictors of $Y$ "
"breaks the logic of the causal graph. Because a standard regression "
"implicitly assumes that each predictor explains variation in $Y$ "
"**conditional on the others**, not respecting causal direction. "
"Mathematically, the estimated coefficients $(\\hat\\beta_1, "
"\\hat\\beta_4)$ in"
msgstr ""
"Una regresión que incluye tanto $X_1$ como $X_4$ como predictores de $Y$ "
"rompe la lógica del gráfico causal. Porque una regresión estándar asume "
"implícitamente que cada predictor explica la variación en $Y$ "
"**condicional a los otros**, sin respetar la dirección causal. "
"Matemáticamente, los coeficientes estimados $(\\hat\\beta_1, "
"\\hat\\beta_4)$ en"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:490030
#: 67df8b2fec2f430bab4e5995c490f2bc
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"\n"
"Y_t = \\alpha + \\hat\\beta_1 X_{1,t} + \\hat\\beta_4 X_{4,t} + "
"\\varepsilon_t\n"
msgstr ""
"\n"
"Y_t = \\alpha + \\hat\\beta_1 X_{1,t} + \\hat\\beta_4 X_{4,t} + "
"\\varepsilon_t\n"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:490034
#: e235f6e0a7c84a7c87cdc311e47ef818
msgid ""
"come from minimizing the joint residual variance, i.e., solving the "
"**normal equations**:"
msgstr ""
"proviene de minimizar la varianza residual conjunta, es decir, resolver "
"las **ecuaciones normales**:"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:490036
#: d39a4e5ccc994cf3986787ee63b3cd09
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"\n"
"\\begin{cases}\n"
"\\mathbb{E}[X_1 (Y - \\alpha - \\hat\\beta_1 X_1 - \\hat\\beta_4 X_4)] = "
"0 \\\\\n"
"\\mathbb{E}[X_4 (Y - \\alpha - \\hat\\beta_1 X_1 - \\hat\\beta_4 X_4)] = "
"0\n"
"\\end{cases}\n"
msgstr ""
"\n"
"\\begin{cases}\n"
"\\mathbb{E}[X_1 (Y - \\alpha - \\hat\\beta_1 X_1 - \\hat\\beta_4 X_4)] = "
"0 \\\\\n"
"\\mathbb{E}[X_4 (Y - \\alpha - \\hat\\beta_1 X_1 - \\hat\\beta_4 X_4)] = "
"0\n"
"\\end{cases}\n"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:490043
#: e53a71c001c54cd2b362bf4848083c0c
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"These equations depend not only on the relation between each $X_j$ and "
"$Y$, but also on the **covariance between the predictors** "
"$\\operatorname{Cov}(X_1,X_4)$. Hence, the regression is influenced by "
"**pairwise correlations** among the covariates themselves!"
msgstr ""
"Estas ecuaciones dependen no solo de la relación entre cada $X_j$ y $Y$, "
"sino también de la **covarianza entre los predictores** "
"$\\operatorname{Cov}(X_1,X_4)$. Por lo tanto, la regresión está "
"influenciada por **correlaciones por pares** entre las covariables "
"mismas."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:490045
#: 45bb492635a749ea8c468514e099d3ad
msgid ""
"Because $X_1$ and $X_4$ are strongly correlated (due to the causal chain "
"$X_1 \\to X_4$), and because $Y$ responds **nonlinearly or dynamically** "
"to $X_4$, the regression cannot represent the true relationship $Y = "
"f(X_4)$. The residuals of this misspecification correlate with $X_1$, and"
" part of the nonlinear structure of $f(X_4)$ is then falsely attributed "
"to $X_1$."
msgstr ""
"Porque $X_1$ y $X_4$ están fuertemente correlacionados (debido a la "
"cadena causal $X_1 \\to X_4$), y porque $Y$ responde **no lineal o "
"dinámicamente** a $X_4$, la regresión no puede representar la verdadera "
"relación $Y = f(X_4)$. Los residuos de esta especificación incorrecta se "
"correlacionan con $X_1$, y parte de la estructura no lineal de $f(X_4)$ "
"se atribuye erróneamente a $X_1$."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:490047
#: 96698671ee3a4081b83a3621d436befb
msgid "In effect:"
msgstr "En efecto:"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:490049
#: 85eeb841e14d451fadc644b511ff36f9
msgid "$X_4$ is a **mediator** of $X_1$’s effect."
msgstr "$X_4$ es un **mediador** del efecto de $X_1$."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:490050
#: a2c745271095490bb0767fb0b636bf0c
msgid "Conditioning on $X_4$ **blocks** the true pathway from $X_1$ to $Y$."
msgstr "Condicionar sobre $X_4$ **bloquea** el verdadero camino de $X_1$ a $Y$."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:490051
#: 7d4f4e1b13d640648048168db5d43912
msgid ""
"Because the regression also balances correlations among predictors, any "
"**nonlinear or lagged pattern** in $Y$ that depends on $X_4$ but is not "
"modeled correctly gets **redistributed** among correlated predictors — "
"primarily $X_1$."
msgstr ""
"Debido a que la regresión también equilibra las correlaciones entre los "
"predictores, cualquier **patrón no lineal o rezagado** en $Y$ que dependa"
" de $X_4$ pero que no esté modelado correctamente se **redistribuye** "
"entre los predictores correlacionados, principalmente $X_1$."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:490054
#: 24a473eae33044abade6cdfbc746a70b
msgid ""
"**Mathematical intuition:**   The regression coefficient of $X_1$ is "
"proportional to the **partial covariance**"
msgstr ""
"**Intuición matemática:**   El coeficiente de regresión de $X_1$ es "
"proporcional a la **covarianza parcial**"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:490057
#: 5ffddd20a32e4015adf2858bf6b15308
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"\n"
"\\hat\\beta_1 \\;\\propto\\; \\operatorname{Cov}\\!\\big(X_1,\\,Y \\mid "
"X_4\\big),\n"
msgstr ""
"\n"
"\\hat\\beta_1 \\;\\propto\\; \\operatorname{Cov}\\!\\big(X_1,\\,Y \\mid "
"X_4\\big),\n"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:490061
#: 8396aa3a012d4b42aac027d63a90773c
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"and since $Y$ depends nonlinearly on $X_4$ while $X_1$ and $X_4$ are "
"collinear, $\\operatorname{Cov}(X_1,\\,Y \\mid X_4)$ remains positive "
"even if the true direct effect $X_1\\!\\to\\!Y$ is zero. This creates the"
" illusion of a large direct influence of $X_1$."
msgstr ""
"y dado que $Y$ depende de manera no lineal de $X_4$ mientras que $X_1$ y "
"$X_4$ son colineales, $\\operatorname{Cov}(X_1,\\,Y \\mid X_4)$ permanece"
" positivo incluso si el verdadero efecto directo $X_1\\!\\to\\!Y$ es "
"cero. Esto crea la ilusión de una gran influencia directa de $X_1$."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:490064
#: e37c9f413c334431943c6c080416d8c3
msgid "The backdoor criterion"
msgstr "El criterio de puerta trasera"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:490066
#: ffa3b578a8814d2a93ec958fbd927a33
msgid ""
"All above logic is frame under the **backdoor criterion** which tells us "
"which variables we must (and must not) adjust for to estimate a causal "
"effect correctly."
msgstr ""
"Toda la lógica anterior se enmarca bajo el **criterio de puerta trasera**"
" que nos indica qué variables debemos (y no debemos) ajustar para estimar"
" correctamente un efecto causal."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:490068
#: 8f1293b9d44941e3944c46d9b9470930
msgid "What it means?"
msgstr "¿Qué significa?"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:490070
#: 805f48827b52444ca6e248bfa8449b3c
msgid ""
"A set of variables $Z$ satisfies the backdoor criterion for the effect of"
" $X$ on $Y$ if:"
msgstr ""
"Un conjunto de variables $Z$ satisface el criterio de puerta trasera para"
" el efecto de $X$ sobre $Y$ si:"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:490072
#: e958d71b2ee94d74b3e0623248339978
msgid ""
"None of the variables in $Z$ are **effects of $X$** (they must not lie "
"downstream)."
msgstr ""
"Ninguna de las variables en $Z$ son **efectos de $X$** (no deben estar en"
" la parte posterior)."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:490073
#: 509cc284b1f84683a957d73354c53d79
msgid ""
"Once we control for $Z$, there are **no unblocked paths** that start with"
" an arrow *into* $X$ (these are “backdoor paths” representing "
"confounding)."
msgstr ""
"Una vez que controlamos por $Z$, no hay **caminos desbloqueados** que "
"comiencen con una flecha *hacia* $X$ (estos son \"caminos de puerta "
"trasera\" que representan confusión)."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:490075
#: 692ae44030374d07be65c2667cc0cfe6
msgid ""
"If these two conditions hold, we can identify the causal effect of $X$ on"
" $Y$ by comparing units with different $X$ values **but the same $Z$**."
msgstr ""
"Si se cumplen estas dos condiciones, podemos identificar el efecto causal"
" de $X$ sobre $Y$ comparando unidades con diferentes valores de $X$ "
"**pero el mismo $Z$**."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:490077
#: 449a3a5307a24252b104855be31a5ec2
msgid "In our case"
msgstr "En nuestro caso"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:490079
#: 2ae69f5d26324df7aad1fbbab6307189
msgid "To estimate the causal effect of $X_1$ on $Y$:"
msgstr "Para estimar el efecto causal de $X_1$ sobre $Y$:"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:490081
#: b29ede1d86d04dfb9eebac7e6ff380a3
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"We **should adjust** for background factors that affect both $X_1$ and "
"$Y$ (for example, $\\mathrm{Trend}_t$ or $\\mathrm{Events}_t$)."
msgstr ""
"Debemos **ajustar** los factores de fondo que afectan tanto a $X_1$ como "
"a $Y$ (por ejemplo, $\\mathrm{Trend}_t$ o $\\mathrm{Events}_t$)."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:490082
#: aeb290d1ecc144f1b08303e6f561f9a4
msgid ""
"We **should not adjust** for mediators such as $X_2$, $X_3$, or $X_4$, "
"because these are **effects** of $X_1$."
msgstr ""
"No **debemos ajustar** por mediadores como $X_2$, $X_3$ o $X_4$, porque "
"estos son **efectos** de $X_1$."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:490084
#: 0de10a96323b476fbee549f04cbfb4b1
msgid "Mathematically, the causal effect can be expressed as:"
msgstr "Matemáticamente, el efecto causal puede expresarse como:"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:490086
#: 99cceec0e55d421a95c2f21f0a2b5d59
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"\n"
"\\mathbb{E}[Y_t \\mid \\mathrm{do}(X_{1,t}=x)]\n"
"= \\int \\mathbb{E}[Y_t \\mid X_{1,t}=x, Z_t=z]\\, dP(z),\n"
msgstr ""
"\n"
"\\mathbb{E}[Y_t \\mid \\mathrm{do}(X_{1,t}=x)]\n"
"= \\int \\mathbb{E}[Y_t \\mid X_{1,t}=x, Z_t=z]\\, dP(z),\n"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:490091
#: 6447f7fba3a042c7abdf7342514a57bf
msgid ""
"where $Z_t$ contains only the valid backdoor variables (common causes, "
"not descendants)."
msgstr ""
"donde $Z_t$ contiene únicamente las variables de puerta trasera válidas "
"(causas comunes, no descendientes)."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:490093
#: 3e90135185d449bfb356c12484aa772b
msgid ""
"In this case, this will imply to estimate the effect of $X4$ on $Y$. Then"
" we could estimate the effect of $X1$ on $X4$ and get the propagation of "
"the effect of $X1$ on $Y$ after."
msgstr ""
"En este caso, esto implicará estimar el efecto de $X4$ en $Y$. Luego "
"podríamos estimar el efecto de $X1$ en $X4$ y obtener la propagación del "
"efecto de $X1$ en $Y$ después."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:490095
#: af4150d6a0744780a5b37f3b3dddaa2c
msgid "Mediator model"
msgstr "Modelo de mediador"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:490097
#: 685b1ba9f12d4bcca94f7ea61fe93d0a
msgid ""
"Let's think once more on our dag, $X1$ is the upper funnel channel. $X4$ "
"is the lower funnel channel. $Y$ is the outcome. This means that $X1$ "
"does not have a direct effect on $Y$, but it does have an indirect effect"
" through $X4$. This means, $X4$ mediates the effect of $X1$ on $Y$."
msgstr ""
"Pensemos una vez más en nuestro diagrama, $X1$ es el canal superior del "
"embudo. $X4$ es el canal inferior del embudo. $Y$ es el resultado. Esto "
"significa que $X1$ no tiene un efecto directo sobre $Y$, pero sí tiene un"
" efecto indirecto a través de $X4$. Esto significa que $X4$ media el "
"efecto de $X1$ sobre $Y$."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:490099
#: a77bb74558354f1093db1aff357fd395
msgid ""
"*The minimal adjustment set based on backdoor paths dictates* that we "
"need to estimate the effect of $X4$ on $Y$ easily, a simple linear or "
"nonlinear model $Y = f(\\theta, X4) + \\varepsilon$ would be enough "
"because $X4$ will block all backdoor paths for the rest of variables."
msgstr ""
"*El conjunto de ajuste mínimo basado en caminos de puerta trasera dicta* "
"que, para estimar fácilmente el efecto de $X4$ sobre $Y$, bastaría un modelo"
" lineal o no lineal simple $Y = f(\\theta, X4) + \\varepsilon$, porque $X4$ "
"bloqueará todos los caminos de puerta trasera del resto de las variables."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:510002
#: a8c3e6c2badf4aa78733a7be887975d6
msgid ""
"Lets see if we can recover the true contribution of $X4$ on $Y$. This "
"will be the most essential step to recover the true contribution of $X1$ "
"on $Y$ after. Here, just as before, we can take our pytensor graph and "
"evaluate it with the values of $X4$ and get the true contribution."
msgstr ""
"Veamos si podemos recuperar la verdadera contribución de $X4$ en $Y$. "
"Este será el paso más esencial para recuperar la verdadera contribución "
"de $X1$ en $Y$ después. Aquí, al igual que antes, podemos tomar nuestro "
"gráfico de pytensor y evaluarlo con los valores de $X4$ y obtener la "
"verdadera contribución."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:530002
#: b5d0313ed3684bf08181babbc687abf4
msgid ""
"If this outcome block is faithful, its contributions should trace the "
"simulated truth."
msgstr ""
"Si este bloque de resultado es fiel, sus contribuciones deberían seguir "
"la verdad simulada."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:550002
#: 53d86307081148638891c6524c5de039
msgid ""
"Great, we can observe that the true value was recovered. Now we can move "
"forward and estimate the effect of $(X_1)$ on $(X_4)$. This is the second"
" essential step before quantifying the contribution of $(X_1)$ to $(Y)$."
msgstr ""
"Excelente, podemos observar que se recuperó el valor verdadero. Ahora "
"podemos avanzar y estimar el efecto de $(X_1)$ en $(X_4)$. Este es el "
"segundo paso esencial antes de cuantificar la contribución de $(X_1)$ a "
"$(Y)$."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:550004
#: a58b05b09a0846b09b2b9137e54a6816
msgid ""
"Now, in real life you don't know the true structural form which generates"
" your data, here I'm taking two choices."
msgstr ""
"Ahora, en la vida real no conoces la verdadera forma estructural que "
"genera tus datos, aquí estoy tomando dos elecciones."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:550006
#: 0a54352713094869b7ca674dbd05e84c
msgid "**Modeling choices.**"
msgstr "**Elecciones de modelado.**"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:550007
#: b4af643338874964b1bef69780b5d205
msgid ""
"I temporarily remove adstock and saturation so the $(X_1 \\to X_4)$ "
"relation is linear."
msgstr ""
"Elimino temporalmente el adstock y la saturación para que la relación "
"$(X_1 \\to X_4)$ sea lineal."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:550008
#: 7be0f68491e54e2e84d60073fe57ff29
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"I avoid a levels-on-levels regression like $(X_{4,t} = \\beta\\,X_{1,t} +"
" \\varepsilon_t)$."
msgstr ""
"Evito una regresión de niveles sobre niveles como $(X_{4,t} = "
"\\beta\\,X_{1,t} + \\varepsilon_t)$."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:550010
#: c83a0f7e065240a39fe866d4638e5643
msgid ""
"This could be translate to *I don't think effect of $X1$ saturates or "
"adstock before impact $X4$*."
msgstr ""
"Esto podría traducirse como *No creo que el efecto de $X1$ se sature ni "
"tenga adstock antes de impactar a $X4$*."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:550012
#: b263a1276890438aba9fb5a97e11dfef
msgid "Let's build this model to see if we can recover the true value."
msgstr "Construyamos este modelo para ver si podemos recuperar el valor verdadero."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:570003
#: 79323cfe3b2248f6b8596da6e0bf8947
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"**Why to build a model using the difference between variables?** If "
"$(X_{1,t})$ and $(X_{4,t})$ are $(I(1))$ and *not* cointegrated, the "
"residual from $(X_{4,t} - \\beta X_{1,t})$ remains $(I(1))$. OLS in "
"levels yields invalid inference and a drifting $(\\hat\\beta)$. First-"
"differencing removes unit roots and yields a stationary relation:"
msgstr ""
"**¿Por qué construir un modelo utilizando la diferencia entre "
"variables?** Si $(X_{1,t})$ y $(X_{4,t})$ son $(I(1))$ y *no* están "
"cointegrados, el residuo de $(X_{4,t} - \\beta X_{1,t})$ permanece "
"$(I(1))$. OLS en niveles produce inferencias inválidas y un "
"$(\\hat\\beta)$ que se desvía. La diferenciación primera elimina raíces "
"unitarias y produce una relación estacionaria:"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:570006
#: fd431d215e4b48958529064c7e602f55
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"\n"
"\\Delta X_{4,t} = \\alpha + \\beta\\,\\Delta X_{1,t} + \\eta_t,\n"
msgstr ""
"\n"
"\\Delta X_{4,t} = \\alpha + \\beta\\,\\Delta X_{1,t} + \\eta_t,\n"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:570010
#: 5d7af491921e405b850748704c79442e
msgid ""
"where $(\\eta_t)$ is $(I(0))$. Under standard exogeneity of innovations, "
"OLS consistently estimates the **total instantaneous effect** $(\\beta)$ "
"of $(X_1)$ on $(X_4)$. In practice, $\\alpha \\neq 0$ because drifts in "
"the level processes translate into a nonzero mean in differences."
msgstr ""
"donde $(\\eta_t)$ es $(I(0))$. Bajo la exogeneidad estándar de las "
"innovaciones, OLS estima consistentemente el **efecto instantáneo total** "
"$(\\beta)$ de $(X_1)$ sobre $(X_4)$. En la práctica, $\\alpha \\neq 0$ "
"porque las derivas en los procesos de nivel se traducen en una media no nula"
" en las diferencias."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:570013
#: 8bdc975bf5c54493bd7d3a344cfd0985
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"We can plot the posterior distribution of the beta to see if the true "
"value was recovered. Because the data generation process is linear, we "
"can calculate the true coefficient of $x1$ over $x4$ doing ( "
"$\\beta_{1,2} * \\beta_{2,4} * \\beta_{1,3} * \\beta_{3,4}$ )"
msgstr ""
"Podemos trazar la distribución posterior del beta para ver si se recuperó"
" el valor verdadero. Dado que el proceso de generación de datos es "
"lineal, podemos calcular el coeficiente verdadero de $x1$ sobre $x4$ "
"haciendo ( $\\beta_{1,2} * \\beta_{2,4} * \\beta_{1,3} * \\beta_{3,4}$ )"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:590002
#: 1cc0c59ec6c940618d42801a4a61516d
msgid ""
"The posterior settles near the ground truth—which is what we’d hope if "
"our story is coherent. Now, what? Armed with the mediated beta, we "
"translate awareness into downstream pressure over time, in‑sample and "
"beyond."
msgstr ""
"El posterior se establece cerca de la verdad fundamental, que es lo que "
"esperaríamos si nuestra historia es coherente. Ahora, ¿qué? Armados con "
"la beta mediada, traducimos la conciencia en presión descendente a lo "
"largo del tiempo, dentro de la muestra y más allá."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:590004
#: 48bff88b81084497a8f83a6774e501c0
msgid ""
"Let's create the xarray with proper broadcasting for chain, draw, date "
"dimensions."
msgstr ""
"Creemos el xarray con la difusión adecuada para las dimensiones de "
"cadena, dibujo y fecha."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:610002
#: 57a9463ec0514ebb8e4dd3b3eb89acc7
msgid ""
"Now, we got the estimated contribution of $X1$ on $X4$. Let's plot "
"against the true contribution of $X1$ on $X4$."
msgstr ""
"Ahora, tenemos la contribución estimada de $X1$ sobre $X4$. Vamos a "
"graficar en comparación con la verdadera contribución de $X1$ sobre $X4$."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:630002
#: e0e6395e06c04f538a293e5ffc1bb00d
msgid ""
"Great, we can see that the estimated contribution is very close to the "
"true contribution in the in-sample period. We can do the same for the "
"out-of-sample period, and using the out of sample period, we can check if"
" we recovered the causal effect of $X1$ on $Y$."
msgstr ""
"Excelente, podemos ver que la contribución estimada está muy cerca de la "
"verdadera contribución en el período de muestra. Podemos hacer lo mismo "
"para el período fuera de muestra, y utilizando el período fuera de "
"muestra, podemos verificar si recuperamos el efecto causal de $X1$ sobre "
"$Y$."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:650002
#: fb8865a352a840e18c9e12d5a2b9d434
msgid ""
"This estimations tell us how much $X1$ is contributing to $X4$ in the "
"out-of-sample period. If we want to ask the causal question, we need a "
"counterfactual: What would $X4$ have been if awareness had gone to zero? "
"We can do this by taking the original value of $X4$ and subtracting the "
"estimated contribution of $X1$ on $X4$."
msgstr ""
"Estas estimaciones nos indican cuánto está contribuyendo $X1$ a $X4$ en "
"el período fuera de muestra. Si queremos plantear la pregunta causal, "
"necesitamos un contrafactual: ¿Qué habría sido $X4$ si la concienciación "
"hubiera llegado a cero? Podemos hacer esto tomando el valor original de "
"$X4$ y restando la contribución estimada de $X1$ sobre $X4$."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:670002
#: 951a8cf7cf824c30aaf5224439f9797d
msgid ""
"We send that counterfactual $X_4$ under $do(X_1=0)$ through the outcome "
"model to obtain $Y$ under $do(X_1=0)$ as consequence. Then the causal "
"effect will be $Y|do(X_1=1) - Y|do(X_1=0)$."
msgstr ""
"Enviamos ese contrafactual $X_4$ bajo $do(X_1=0)$ a través del modelo de "
"resultados para obtener $Y$ bajo $do(X_1=0)$ como consecuencia. Entonces,"
" el efecto causal será $Y|do(X_1=1) - Y|do(X_1=0)$."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:670004
#: 3325f88e406648219b65d3e97637e4ed
msgid ""
"We'll compute the true influence of $X_1$ on $Y$ by our true pytensor "
"graph, and finally, we'll compare the recovered effect with the true "
"effect."
msgstr ""
"Calcularemos la verdadera influencia de $X_1$ sobre $Y$ mediante nuestro "
"verdadero gráfico de pytensor y, finalmente, compararemos el efecto "
"recuperado con el efecto verdadero."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:700002
#: 49733a3e01f6438f99deaa9e621904e9
msgid "Let's plot the recovered effect against the true effect, side‑by‑side."
msgstr ""
"Vamos a trazar el efecto recuperado frente al efecto verdadero, uno al "
"lado del otro."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:720002
#: 0364250afcad444c8af260b30e146843
msgid ""
"This is great, we can see that the recovered effect is very close to the "
"true effect in the in-sample period. We can do the same for the out-of-"
"sample period, and using the out of sample period, we observe the causal "
"effect of $X1$ on $Y$ was properly recovered."
msgstr ""
"Esto es excelente, podemos ver que el efecto recuperado está muy cerca "
"del efecto verdadero en el período de muestra. Podemos hacer lo mismo "
"para el período fuera de muestra, y utilizando el período fuera de "
"muestra, observamos que el efecto causal de $X1$ sobre $Y$ fue "
"correctamente recuperado."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:720004
#: 54c2725ea37141ae9d07f59769ef5753
msgid "Conclusion"
msgstr "Conclusión"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:720006
#: efb265eb9b654ea1bfa20583cb28c01e
msgid ""
"In this tutorial we showed that it is possible to recover high‑level, "
"upper‑funnel impacts even when the observed target is a lower‑funnel KPI."
" By explicitly modeling mediation and then propagating that signal "
"through the outcome model, we captured the causal contribution of "
"upper‑funnel activity from low‑level targets."
msgstr ""
"En este tutorial mostramos que es posible recuperar impactos de alto "
"nivel y de embudo superior incluso cuando el objetivo observado es un KPI"
" de embudo inferior. Al modelar explícitamente la mediación y luego "
"propagar esa señal a través del modelo de resultados, capturamos la "
"contribución causal de la actividad de embudo superior a partir de "
"objetivos de bajo nivel."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:720008
#: 33234601a11842f19754907e02fd7350
msgid ""
"**Estimate mediated effect**: quantify the link from awareness to a "
"downstream mediator and recover its contribution."
msgstr ""
"**Efecto mediado estimado**: cuantificar el vínculo desde la conciencia "
"hasta un mediador posterior y recuperar su contribución."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:720009
#: f5c165db3a6d4feba31c07a25565da36
msgid ""
"**Propagate to outcomes**: translate the mediated effect into expected "
"pressure on the final target via the MMM."
msgstr ""
"**Propagar a resultados**: traducir el efecto mediado en la presión "
"esperada sobre el objetivo final a través del MMM."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:720010
#: e1d41b0fe8e74af1a975f023ba407ee2
msgid ""
"**Causal counterfactuals**: compare against do‑operator counterfactuals "
"to measure upper‑funnel lift credibly."
msgstr ""
"**Contrafactuales causales**: comparar con contrafactuales del operador "
"do para medir de manera creíble el aumento en la parte superior del "
"embudo."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach.ipynb:720012
#: 6881fd5419cb4b65949f575264a5ff59
msgid ""
"This makes upper‑funnel value measurable alongside performance channels, "
"improving attribution, forecasting, and budget decisions while keeping "
"the model grounded in causal structure."
msgstr ""
"Esto hace que el valor del embudo superior sea medible junto con los "
"canales de rendimiento, mejorando la atribución, la previsión y las "
"decisiones presupuestarias, mientras mantiene el modelo fundamentado en "
"una estructura causal."

